Subject: [PATCH] 4423: an assistant-only answer to a helper's question is not
 a question (switch OFF)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 51382: a helper asked the owner a clarifying question, the owner's
assistant answered it by itself (1688 part 1), and the answer went out as
a question back. With ANSWER_NOT_QUESTION_ON, createAsk refuses such a
reply — the helper's last answer ended with „?", nobody typed in between
(isAssistantOnlyRound), and the reply ends with „?" too — and the run is
told to state what the owner said, or to ask the owner first.

The note is model-facing text (D44), so the switch is OFF until Misho's
yes on its exact words (NIGHT_QUESTIONS BL). With it OFF nothing changes:
the live ask row now also reads its answer, which only the gate uses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
